# Condition 5 of BACKEND-PLAN.md §0.3.1: api/app/security/ is a protected path so that
# changes there get a deliberate second read rather than a drive-by edit. Working solo,
# the value is the forced pause, not the second person.
#
# ACTION REQUIRED: replace @OWNER with the real GitHub username or team. A CODEOWNERS file
# with a non-existent owner silently protects nothing — GitHub assigns nobody, the review
# rule never fires, and the repository looks protected in exactly the way it is not.
#
# This is no longer a comment asking someone to remember. `api/tools/check_codeowners.py`
# runs in CI and FAILS while @OWNER is still here. It is expected to be red until this repo
# has a real owner on GitHub, and that is the point: a control that has not been switched on
# should say so, not sit quietly looking finished.
#
# Also required by BACKEND-PLAN.md §0.3.1 condition 5, which is why the security paths below
# are listed individually rather than relying on the catch-all.

*                           @OWNER

# The auth and security surface. Phases 5 and 6 carry more risk than the other fifteen
# combined (§0.3), and these are the files where a forgotten line is invisible from the
# outside.
/api/app/security/          @OWNER
/api/app/config.py          @OWNER
/api/app/logging.py         @OWNER

# The gates themselves. Weakening a check is how a check stops working.
/api/tools/                 @OWNER
/.github/workflows/         @OWNER

# The decision record and the dependency allowlist.
/postgame/BACKEND-PLAN.md   @OWNER
/postgame/DEPENDENCIES.md   @OWNER
